ime":0.16,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":"0.3","y":"0","z":"-0.12"}],"uuid":"41bc93d1-fa61-53e8-9e64-78604af6661d","time":0.22,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"},{"channel":"position","data_points":[{"x":"0","y":"0","z":"0"}],"uuid":"57ed1703-b34c-5dbc-9171-0693bb3abc35","time":0.3,"color":-1,"interpolation":"linear"}]}}}],"description":"# rock_coal\n\nCoal rock (remade in Patch 5): a grey rock of overlapping blocks with twelve black glossy coal chunks of different sizes and angles, each sunk at least a third into the rock.\n\n- Bounds (first set): x -47..45, y 0..45, z -38..38 units. Origin at the base centre, front faces -Z.\n- Texture: 256 x 256, 1 px per unit, flat pixel-art tones per material.\n- Cubes: 31 (full 24, depleted 7).\n- Clips: `hit`.\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `full` (visible by default)\n- `depleted`: a low broken stump with rubble and one coal fleck"}